PixelFerry includes private CoreGraphics API declarations and implementation
patterns derived from these MIT-licensed projects:

- DeskPad, copyright Bastian Andelefski and contributors
  https://github.com/Stengo/DeskPad
- VirtualDisplayKit, copyright Dustin Nielson and contributors
  https://github.com/xocialize/VirtualDisplayKit

Their copyright notices are preserved in PixelFerry's LICENSE file.
Deskreen is AGPL-3.0 and was consulted only for high-level architectural
research; its code is not incorporated into this implementation.

The experimental native backend depends on WebRTC binaries packaged by
stasel/WebRTC and on the
Swifter HTTP/WebSocket server. Both are distributed under BSD 3-Clause terms;
their full license notices are available in the dependency distributions.

PixelFerry Streamer uses Electron, Express, Socket.IO, simple-peer,
pixelmatch, and esbuild. Their notices are available in installed npm packages.
It is an original implementation and does not incorporate Deskreen code.
